@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Share Link Mutations
  "Creates and re-points share symlinks and patches the authoritative manifest without moving blob bytes."

  Provides:
    - links.Service @source("symbol:Service")
    - links.NewService @source("symbol:NewService")
    - links.ShareRequest @source("symbol:ShareRequest")
    - links.ShareResult @source("symbol:ShareResult")
    - links.Service.EnsureShare @source("symbol:EnsureShare")

  Consumes:
    - remote.ManifestStore
    - remote.EnsureSafeSymlink
    - domain.Manifest.DecideShare
    - domain.MintSlug

  Invariants:
    - EnsureShare MUST require the blob to already exist in the manifest (two-phase share)
    - New shares MUST mint a slug, reserve it, and create object-path plus canonical and bare slug symlinks
    - Repoint MUST update symlinks only for endpoints still in EndpointOK state
    - Symlink targets MUST stay relative to each link parent directory under the site root

  OutOfScope:
    - Blob byte upload (owned by the share package)
    - mv, cp, rm, disable, enable, prune commands (future links mutations)

  Scenario (happy-path): Create new share
    Given a manifest with the blob recorded but no share at the object path
    When EnsureShare runs
    Then Action is ShareCreate, symlinks are written, and manifest is committed

  Scenario (happy-path): No-op same blob
    Given an object path already pointing at the same blob
    When EnsureShare runs
    Then Action is ShareNoop and no manifest write occurs

  Scenario (negative): Blob not uploaded
    Given a blob key absent from manifest.Blobs
    When EnsureShare runs
    Then it returns an error instructing the caller to upload first
